---
title: "get_application_status GET /v1/integration/rounds/{id}/application (Legion Backend API)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_auth: api_key = headers["x-api-key"]
    q_auth --> q_check_key: api_key valid
    q_check_key --> q_sign: identifier = round_id or user_id
    q_check_key --> q_reject: api_key invalid
    q_reject --> [*]: revert "unauthorized"
    q_sign --> q_compute_sig: signature = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, identifier)
    q_compute_sig --> q_send: GET /v1/integration/rounds/{id}/application with X-Signature
    q_send --> q_parse: response = server_response
    q_parse --> q_found: response.status == 2xx
    q_parse --> q_not_found: no application exists
    q_parse --> q_error: response.status == other error
    q_found --> [*]: return application_status
    q_not_found --> [*]: revert "application not found"
    q_error --> [*]: revert "status check failed"

    note right of q_found
        INV-001: application status reflects current state (pending, approved, rejected, etc.)
        INV-002: status query is read-only and does not modify application state
        INV-003: user can only view their own application status (authorization check)
    end note
